    "fullDescription": "# Rajasthan Vidyut Vibhag LDC Syllabus 2026 & Exam Pattern\n\nRajasthan Rajya Vidyut Utpadan Nigam Limited (RVUNL) conducts recruitment for Lower Division Clerk (LDC) / Junior Assistant across various power companies in Rajasthan, including RVUNL, RVPNL, JVVNL, AVVNL, and JDVVNL. Candidates preparing for the examination must go through the detailed exam pattern and syllabus.\n\n## Exam Selection Process\n\n1. Phase I: Written Competitive Exam (Computer Based Test)\n2. Phase II: Computer Proficiency Test (Speed & Efficiency Test)\n3. Document Verification & Medical Examination\n\n## Exam Pattern Phase 1 (Written Exam)\n\n- **Mode of Exam:** Online Computer Based Test (CBT)\n- **Duration:** 2 Hours (120 Minutes)\n- **Question Type:** Objective Multiple Choice Questions (MCQs)\n- **Subjects Covered:** Reasoning & Mental Ability, General Knowledge & Everyday Science, General Hindi, General English, Mathematics.\n\n## Phase 2 (Computer Proficiency Test)\n\n- **Speed Test:** Hindi & English Typing Test (15 Minutes each)\n- **Efficiency Test:** Test on Microsoft Word, Excel, and basic computer functions (15 Minutes)",
    "faqs": [
      {
        "question": "What is the educational qualification for Rajasthan Vidyut Vibhag LDC 2026?",
        "answer": "Candidates must possess a Bachelor's Degree in any stream along with an RS-CIT or equivalent computer qualification."
      },
      {
        "question": "Is there any negative marking in the written examination?",
        "answer": "Yes, standard negative marking (usually 1/4th mark) applies for wrong answers in the written test."
      },
      {
        "question": "What is the age limit for RVUNL LDC Recruitment?",
        "answer": "The minimum age is 18 years and the maximum age limit is 40 years, with category-wise relaxations."
      },
      {
        "question": "What subjects are included in the LDC written exam?",
        "answer": "The exam covers Reasoning, Mathematics, General Knowledge, Everyday Science, General Hindi, and General English."
      },
      {
        "question": "Is computer typing test mandatory for selection?",
        "answer": "Yes, candidates who qualify Phase 1 must appear for the Phase 2 Typing and Efficiency Test."
      },
      {
        "question": "What is the typing speed required for LDC?",
        "answer": "Candidates must achieve a minimum speed of 25-30 words per minute in Hindi and English."
      },
      {
        "question": "Can final year students apply for the post?",
        "answer": "Yes, provided they produce proof of passing before the document verification date."
      },
      {
        "question": "Where can I download the LDC Syllabus PDF?",
        "answer": "You can download the full syllabus directly from the official website or the link provided on StudyGovtHelp.in."
      },
      {
        "question": "What is the pay scale for RVUNL LDC / Junior Assistant?",
        "answer": "Selected candidates are placed in Pay Matrix Level L-5 with a probation stipend during the initial 2 years."
      },
      {
        "question": "How many power distribution companies are included in this recruitment?",
        "answer": "Five companies: RVUNL, RVPNL, JVVNL, AVVNL, and JDVVNL."
      }
    ],
