    "keyHighlights": [
      "Phase-III targets the consolidation of 1,25,000 kilometers of existing rural road networks.",
      "Special financial sharing ratio of 90:10 for North Eastern and Himalayan states.",
      "Integration with digital asset management systems for real-time maintenance tracking."
    ],
    "fullContent": "The Union Cabinet, chaired by the Prime Minister, has greenlit the implementation of Pradhan Mantri Gram Sadak Yojana (PMGSY) Phase-III. This phase is strategically designed to upgrade the rural infrastructure by transforming existing rural routes into all-weather, high-specification roads connecting critical rural habitations to Gramin Agricultural Markets (GrAMs), higher secondary schools, and hospitals. Since its inception, PMGSY has served as the backbone of rural connectivity. Phase-III specifically targets the consolidation of 1,25,000 kilometers of rural roads. The funding pattern for this phase follows a 60:40 split between the Central and State Governments for general states, while a liberalized 90:10 ratio is applicable for North Eastern and Himalayan states. Furthermore, the government has mandated the use of green technologies, including plastic waste and cold-mix technology, in road construction under Phase-III to ensure environmental sustainability. A dedicated mobile application will also be deployed to monitor project execution, ensuring transparency and accountability at the grassroots level. This initiative holds immense significance for aspirants preparing for UPSC and State PSC exams, particularly under rural development and governance sections.",
