    "fullContent": "India's strategic focus on ocean and polar science has intensified significantly over recent years, driven by the need to understand changing climate patterns and harness marine resources sustainably. The Ministry of Earth Sciences spearheads major initiatives, including the ambitious Deep Ocean Mission, which underscores India's capabilities in deep-sea exploration and marine technology development. In the polar regions, India has maintained a robust scientific presence for decades. The Antarctic expeditions, which began in the early 1980s, have yielded vital data on global climate systems, ice-core dynamics, and ecological changes. Research stations such as Maitri and Bharati serve as crucial hubs for multidisciplinary studies in the frozen continent. Simultaneously, India's engagement in the Arctic has grown steadily. Station Himadri in Svalbard facilitates year-round studies on Arctic glaciers, fjord dynamics, and atmospheric phenomena. These polar and oceanic initiatives not only enhance India's scientific footprint globally but also contribute valuable insights into monsoon dynamics and sea-level rise affecting the Indian subcontinent.",
