    "fullContent": "### Economic Report Overview In its latest **Global Economic Prospects** report published on 11 August 2026, the World Bank upgraded India's real Gross Domestic Product (GDP) growth forecast for the financial year 2026-27 (FY27) to **7.2%**, up 40 basis points from its earlier estimate of 6.8%. ### Primary Growth Drivers Highlighted 1. **Public Infrastructure Spending:** Continued multi-year capital outlay by the Central Government via the *National Infrastructure Pipeline (NIP)* and *PM Gati Shakti* framework has crowded in private capital investments. 2. **Services and High-Tech Exports:** Strong performance in Global Capability Centres (GCCs), IT services, and high-value manufacturing under Production Linked Incentive (PLI) schemes. 3. **Rural Demand Recovery:** Normal monsoon conditions and stable agricultural productivity boosted real rural incomes and private consumption. ### Macroeconomic Indicators - **Consumer Price Index (CPI) Inflation:** Expected to moderate to **4.1%** in FY27, aligned with the RBI's medium-term mandate of 4% (+/- 2%). - **Current Account Deficit (CAD):** Projected to remain manageable at **1.2% of GDP** due to resilient service trade surpluses and steady remittance inflows. ### Exam Relevance - **World Bank Flagship Reports:** *Global Economic Prospects*, *World Development Report*. - **World Bank HQ:** Washington D.C., USA. - **Exam Target:** Essential for UPSC GS-III (Indian Economy), RBI Grade B, SEBI Grade A, and SBI PO exams.",
