    "fullContent": "### Campaign Triumph in Bangkok India achieved a historical sporting milestone on 11 August 2026 by securing the top spot in the overall medal tally at the **26th Asian Athletics Championships**, held in Bangkok, Thailand. This marks only the second time in history that India has finished at the apex of this prestigious continental championship. ### Top Performers and Key Highlights - **Men's Javelin Throw:** Olympic champion Neeraj Chopra secured Gold with an impressive throw of **89.45 metres**, establishing a new championship record. - **Women's Relay Success:** The team comprising Jyothika Sri Dandi, Subha Venkatesan, Vithya Ramraj, and Animesh Kujur won Gold in the 4x400m relay with a record-setting time of **3:27.14**. - **Middle-Distance Dominance:** Harmilan Bains clinched double Gold in the Women’s 800m and 1500m events. - **Shot Put:** Tajinderpal Singh Toor captured his third consecutive Asian Championship Gold medal with a throw of 20.82 metres. ### Final Tally Comparison 1. **India:** 12 Gold, 9 Silver, 8 Bronze (29 Total) 2. **China:** 10 Gold, 11 Silver, 7 Bronze (28 Total) 3. **Japan:** 8 Gold, 10 Silver, 9 Bronze (27 Total) ### Exam Relevance - **Governing Body:** Athletics Federation of India (AFI) headquartered in New Delhi. - **Exam Target:** Important for sports awards, GK sections in SSC CGL, Banking Awareness, RRB NTPC, and State Public Service Exams.",
