    "fullContent": "### RBI Directive and Technical Framework On 11 August 2026, the Reserve Bank of India (RBI) issued an updated regulatory operational framework governing the Central Bank Digital Currency (CBDC), widely known as the **Digital Rupee (e₹)**. The new framework officially expands the scope of both retail (e₹-R) and wholesale (e₹-W) segments by introducing two groundbreaking features: **offline transaction capability** and **programmability**. ### Key Features of the Enhanced Framework 1. **Offline Payments:** Utilizing Near Field Communication (NFC) and secure hardware elements within mobile devices, users can perform instant token-based transactions without active cellular data or internet connection. 2. **Programmable Smart Tokens:** Central and state government entities can issue targeted e₹ tokens with embedded smart contracts. For instance, agricultural input subsidies (fertilizer/seed vouchers) can be programmed so that funds are spendable only at registered agricultural dealers. 3. **UPI Integration:** Complete interoperability ensures that any merchant standard UPI QR code can seamlessly process e₹-R payments directly into user wallets. ### Exam Relevance & Facts - **Legal Basis:** Section 22 of the Reserve Bank of India Act, 1934 (amended via the Finance Act 2022 to include digital currency). - **CBDC Launch:** Retail pilot initially launched on 1 December 2022. - **Competitive Exam Focus:** Critical for RBI Grade B, NABARD, IBPS PO, and UPSC GS-III (Indian Economy, Monetary Policy).",
    "source": "GK Today",
    "sourceUrl": "",
    "publishedAt": "11 August 2026",
