    "fullContent": "### Summit Overview and Key Deliberations The 18th East Asia Summit (EAS) concluded on 11 August 2026 in Vientiane, Laos, bringing together leaders from the 10 ASEAN member states and eight dialogue partners: India, the United States, China, Russia, Japan, South Korea, Australia, and New Zealand. ### Strategic Highlights and Declaration The summit adopted the **Vientiane Declaration on Maritime Cooperation and Economic Resilience**, emphasizing freedom of navigation, peaceful dispute resolution under the 1982 United Nations Convention on the Law of the Sea (UNCLOS), and unhindered maritime commerce. Key discussion areas included: - **Indo-Pacific Alignment:** Highlighting convergence between the *ASEAN Outlook on the Indo-Pacific (AOIP)* and India’s *Indo-Pacific Oceans Initiative (IPOI)*. - **Supply Chain Security:** Agreement to establish an emergency response mechanism for semiconductor and critical mineral supply chain disruptions. - **Digital Framework:** Rollout of the East Asia Digital Connectivity Initiative aimed at harmonizing digital payment infrastructure among member states. ### Exam Relevance - **EAS Composition:** 18 countries (10 ASEAN + 8 Dialogue Partners). - **First EAS Summit:** Held in Kuala Lumpur, Malaysia, in December 2005. - **Exam Application:** Crucial topic for UPSC GS-II (International Relations, Regional Groupings) and SSC/Bank PO GA sections regarding international forums.",
