    "fullContent": "### Diplomatic Gesture India has gifted five peacocks to the **United Nations Office at Geneva (UNOG)** as part of ongoing cultural and diplomatic outreach initiatives. ### Historic Setting The birds will live in **Ariana Park**, the sprawling 45-hectare grounds that encircle the Palais des Nations. The park has historically hosted peacocks since the land was gifted to the city of Geneva with the condition that peacocks be allowed to roam freely. ### Significance * Represents national pride, as the peacock is India's national bird. * Highlights soft-power diplomacy and international friendship. * Strengthens India's diplomatic presence within international multilateral institutions.",
